d read $HOME/.codex/auth.json, /etc/hostname and ~/.ssh, and sandbox_permissions=[] did not close it. A prompt-injected paragraph that persuades the judge to read a host file and return it in reason has a path into the committed judge.json. No exploit was attempted and no live judge call was made. No CLI-level read-deny knob exists, so the remedy is a tool-free model transport or an OS-level mount namespace, 1 to 3 days, out of scope for 102.","USAGE SPANS TWO SESSIONS and the usage object covers only this one. This session (4cda20c9-0c7c-4816-bd83-4622b9ce5f01, claude-opus-5) is the captured object below: 72,340,935 input, 267,229 output, 50.45 USD. The predecessor session (5933a8ff-74fa-46fa-b0a5-332f303b1bae, claude-fable-5-1) spent a further 36,175,316 input and 303,261 output, 66.46 USD, captured as capture_status derived against claude_docs/.wf2-state/102/usage_checkpoint.json at run-id f321bc4c. The two were NOT summed and relabelled, because a hand-sum presented as one capture is the laundering 363 forbids. Whole-run cost is the sum of the two figures stated here.","record-child-outcome returned outcome=no_state_file, fail-open: no campaign under ./claude_docs/.driver-state names issue 102, so nothing was written. Expected for a standalone WF2 run rather than an epic child; recorded because a fail-open with no trace is how a real miss comes to look deliberate.","CI skipped 2 tests that pass on this host: 766 passed and 4 skipped in CI against 768 passed and 2 skipped locally, with 770 collected both times, so no test is missing. INFERRED, not confirmed: the two extra skips are the xattr-gated cases at tests/test_apply_hardening.py:178 and :183, which are pre-existing and unrelated to 102. Confirming it needs -rs added to the workflow gate step, which currently runs pytest tests/ -q.","Two product limitations surfaced and recorded in the results and design documents rather than filed, per the review-finding throttle: a review-stage edit on any invariant-beari